    {
        "id": "en:word:structure-even-though",
        "label": "even though",
        "fields": {
            "part_of_speech": "conjunction",
            "pronunciation": ["/ˈiːvən ðəʊ/"],
            "audio": "audio/2f0d35460f674de7852bcba603b704f1cf26dc881e295496f4340f45177d1cd9.wav",
            "reference_images": [
                "images/f736ea3a71c4c9da6c89da1bd070b3819d0862a02663de888cfbe3986c68fc1b.jpg"
            ],
            "usage_notes": {
                "en": "Even though emphasizes contrast with a fact. Example: Even though he is tired, he keeps walking. The hiker really is tired; compare even if for an uncertain condition.",
                "de": "Even though betont den Gegensatz zu einer Tatsache. „Even though he is tired, he keeps walking.“ = Obwohl er müde ist, geht er weiter. Der Wanderer ist wirklich müde; even if verwendet man bei einer ungewissen Bedingung.",
                "id": "Even though menekankan pertentangan dengan fakta. “Even though he is tired, he keeps walking.” = Meskipun lelah, dia terus berjalan. Pendaki itu benar-benar lelah; bandingkan even if untuk kondisi yang belum pasti.",
                "ja": "even thoughは事実との対比を強調します。「Even though he is tired, he keeps walking.」＝彼は疲れているにもかかわらず歩き続けます。実際に疲れています。不確かな条件を表すeven ifと比べてください。"
            }
        },
        "class": "lexical:conjunction",
        "tags": ["conjunction", "sentence-structure", "grammar"],
