    {
        "id": "en:word:structure-so-that",
        "label": "so that",
        "fields": {
            "part_of_speech": "conjunction",
            "pronunciation": ["/səʊ ðæt/"],
            "audio": "audio/1278d8b029d2bfbe142f7e1ab8379ab30a18ac139ff78e366219d410638760f6.wav",
            "reference_images": [
                "images/11505b07ed6a920d9f8e5c6bcb27e750d0dc4d205fc6c0b7748968a418c9db59.jpg"
            ],
            "usage_notes": {
                "en": "So that can express purpose with a clause. Example: He lifts the child so that the child can reach the jar. The second clause states the intended result.",
                "de": "So that kann mit einem Nebensatz einen Zweck ausdrücken. „He lifts the child so that the child can reach the jar.“ = Er hebt das Kind hoch, damit es das Glas erreichen kann. Der zweite Teilsatz nennt das beabsichtigte Ergebnis.",
                "id": "So that dapat menyatakan tujuan melalui sebuah klausa. “He lifts the child so that the child can reach the jar.” = Dia mengangkat anak itu agar anak itu dapat meraih stoples. Klausa kedua menyatakan hasil yang diinginkan.",
                "ja": "so thatは節を伴って目的を表せます。「He lifts the child so that the child can reach the jar.」＝子どもが瓶に手を届かせられるように、彼は子どもを抱き上げます。後半の節は意図した結果です。"
            }
        },
        "class": "lexical:conjunction",
        "tags": ["conjunction", "sentence-structure", "grammar"],
