    {
        "id": "en:word:structure-unless",
        "label": "unless",
        "fields": {
            "part_of_speech": "conjunction",
            "pronunciation": ["/ənˈles/"],
            "audio": "audio/d2471534afd4a4500d55230db8bb06882ecea307811fbf878e4eed409ccd7125.wav",
            "reference_images": [
                "images/5ec40974a15d93bd57610d7f8cdd9d74a8ad49bb795015fd96988758aad9c2ac.jpg"
            ],
            "usage_notes": {
                "en": "Unless means except if. Example: We will go outside unless it rains. Rain is the exception that would stop the plan; the crossed-out cloud is a cue for that condition.",
                "de": "Unless bedeutet außer wenn. „We will go outside unless it rains.“ = Wir gehen nach draußen, es sei denn, es regnet. Regen ist die Ausnahme, die den Plan verhindern würde; die durchgestrichene Wolke weist darauf hin.",
                "id": "Unless berarti kecuali jika. “We will go outside unless it rains.” = Kami akan keluar kecuali jika hujan. Hujan adalah pengecualian yang akan membatalkan rencana; awan yang dicoret menjadi petunjuk kondisi itu.",
                "ja": "unlessは「〜の場合を除いて」です。「We will go outside unless it rains.」＝雨が降らなければ外に出ます。雨は計画を取りやめる例外で、打ち消された雲はその条件の手がかりです。"
            }
        },
